  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe cause is not \"hundreds of hashes in one run\". Readings in the build worktree `issue-917` (read only):\n\n- The 634 `camcraft-app` unit directories are 627 distinct targets. Each integration test binary (about 620 suites) is one unit with its exe and pdb, about 100 MB. One set is about 64 GB.\n- The growth comes from variants across trees and env. `camcraft-motion` has 747 units for 124 targets, `camcraft-post` 554 for 110, `camcraft-sim` 462 for 92. The variants differ in the profile hash (env before #3154) or in the dependency fingerprints (other `serde_core` feature sets). `Cargo.lock` and the manifests were the same at `8b4209215` and `cc04d7bcd`.\n- Cargo never removes a superseded variant. So each change of env or feature resolution adds a full set.\n\nThe fix (`xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs`, called from the gate summary in `exec.rs`):\n\n- At the end of each run (not a dry run), the gate removes a unit directory only when all of these are true:\n  - it is under `target/{debug,release}/build/` of the gate's own root, and no `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` / `CARGO_BUILD_TARGET_DIR` / `CARGO_BUILD_BUILD_DIR` is set;\n  - its target fingerprint is `test-lib-`, `test-integration-test-` or `test-bin-`;\n  - this run wrote a newer variant of the same target, and this variant is older than the run start.\n- Libraries, binaries and build scripts are never removed. The newest variant is never removed.\n- The sweep does nothing when a cargo lock of the profile directory is held, or when another process names `<root>/target` in its command line. A process list that cannot be read also stops the sweep.\n- A failed delete is a warning line, not a gate failure.\n- The summary prints the number of directories and the GB removed, or why the sweep did not run.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off` (or `0`) turns the sweep off.\n- `seed::lock` is now `pub(crate)`, so that the sweep uses the same lock probe.\n- The `gate` skill has one new paragraph.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3169-gate-unit-sweep.md` (cause, rule, why at the end in any outcome, why only test-harness units, what was dropped).\n\n## Tests\n\n`cargo test -p xtask`: 262 passed in the unit binary, plus the other xtask binaries green. `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. Pinning tests in `xtask/src/unit_sweep_tests.rs`:\n\n- `an_older_variant_of_a_target_built_in_this_run_is_removed_and_the_newest_survives`\n- `two_runs_on_two_trees_leave_one_unit_for_each_target`\n- `no_variant_written_in_this_run_means_nothing_is_removed`\n- `a_non_test_unit_is_never_removed`\n- `a_held_cargo_lock_or_a_live_process_removes_nothing`\n- `superseded_never_lists_the_newest_variant`\n- `the_process_check_finds_another_process_of_this_tree_only`\n- `the_sweep_can_be_turned_off_and_reports_failed_deletes_as_warnings`\n- `the_gate_summary_runs_the_sweep`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real gate run with the sweep on a large target. The real process check (PowerShell `Get-CimInstance` on Windows, `ps` on Unix) ran in no test; the tests use a fake listing and a closure.\n- macOS and Linux are not run.\n- Fewer `camcraft-app` test binaries (the root of the size) is not in this PR. It is in the decision under \"Dropped\".\n\nHeavy lanes: none reached (xtask only).\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3169\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
